<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>BBC News</title><subtitle type="html">BBC News - Technology</subtitle><id>https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:47:10Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss.xml" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/technology" /><link rel="via" href="https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Pornhub investigated over its age checks</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6eq8dw3dlyqo#0</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:46:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:15:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6eq8dw3dlyqo--c37c01db3860.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6eq8dw3dlyqo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The regulator says it has concerns over how the site is relying on third party checks provided by Apple for some users.</summary></entry><entry><title>OpenAI gives cyber defence tools to Ukraine</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c90kly26d7pzo#0</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T12:01:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c90kly26d7pzo--b7e58b5f1e58.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c90kly26d7pzo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Ukraine will get access to OpenAI's advanced GPT 5.6 Sol model under the deal - a rival to Anthropic's Mythos and Fable</summary></entry><entry><title>US criticises Australia's proposed algorithm opt-out laws as 'censorship'</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqj3dgy8x3vro#0</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T01:35:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqj3dgy8x3vro--8189b0d4924d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqj3dgy8x3vro?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Under the draft laws, tech firms face fines if they do not give users the option to switch off algorithms.</summary></entry><entry><title>Will a switch to light speed cut power use at data centres?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c2dwg3zexkpo#0</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T23:03:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c2dwg3zexkpo--43c35a5ce854.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c2dwg3zexkpo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">To save power and add capacity,  data centres are switching from copper wires to tech using light.</summary></entry><entry><title>Huge data centres rise at 'China speed' to power its AI ambitions</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm5ydz4kl65ro#0</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T22:04:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm5ydz4kl65ro--a8ba1405a8aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm5ydz4kl65ro?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The BBC visits Inner Mongolia, an unlikely frontier in Beijing's AI race with Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rare look at the remote engine rooms fuelling China's AI boom</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cwe8ejvv0leno#0</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T22:03:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cwe8ejvv0leno--758c489d1cf9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cwe8ejvv0leno?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The BBC is in Inner Mongolia where dozen of Chinese data centres are being constructed, as the country aims to lead the world in artificial intelligence.</summary></entry><entry><title>Call of Duty's Activision to make next Halo game as Xbox cuts more jobs</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvj64gz74ky4o#0</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:51:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvj64gz74ky4o--3b79a23a7c61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvj64gz74ky4o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The news comes as part of a "reset" announced by Xbox in July, with 3,600 planned job losses overall.</summary></entry><entry><title>Not all AI workers think the tech could kill everyone</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm5y7qj54klpo#0</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T23:01:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm5y7qj54klpo--6c717aa9f7ce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm5y7qj54klpo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">In text exchanges and conversations, multiple people who have worked for leading companies are sceptical of the warnings.</summary></entry><entry><title>Google's Gemini AI hacked three companies in security test</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c607l0k72rlvo#0</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T13:39:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c607l0k72rlvo--0dd033f2a0e6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c607l0k72rlvo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The AI model accessed the internet and guessed credentials to three websites, a Google official told the BBC.</summary></entry><entry><title>Would Australians support a smart glasses ban?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cm9w4nenzv4no#0</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T23:15:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cm9w4nenzv4no--d5911730957e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cm9w4nenzv4no?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">As Australia considers barring the use of smart glasses in government offices, the BBC asks people in Sydney what they think.</summary></entry><entry><title>The virtual worlds where robots are trained</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c79g0j3d4q9o#0</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T23:00:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c79g0j3d4q9o--ca691b64f42f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c79g0j3d4q9o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Training systems that allow robots to negotiate the real world are getting more sophisticated.</summary></entry><entry><title>King Charles warns of 'existential danger' of AI falling into wrong hands</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c65ymj7njvl7o#0</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T14:33:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c65ymj7njvl7o--87edd459c4d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c65ymj7njvl7o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The comments were made at a summit in Ayrshire with participants from AI giants including Nvidia, OpenAI and Anthropic.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why are there concerns AI could threaten humanity, and how real are they?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c790xvnzgnno#0</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T09:18:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c790xvnzgnno--8128fa4f3ef2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c790xvnzgnno?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Existential fears about AI have once again reared their head - here's what you need to know.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyg#2</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:47:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T20:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyg--a5840e5a42f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyg?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">China is competing with the United States and other nations to develop AI.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyf#2</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T19:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyf--0cfb3dcdb81d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyf?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">What should children learn in a world transformed by artificial intelligence?</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyd#2</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T20:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyd--0bf850c7b0e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyd?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Scammers demand money from Instagram users over fake copyright claims.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyc#2</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T20:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyc--aac336945946.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyc?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">AI can only communicate in languages that it's been trained on.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Now</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0032301#3</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T01:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0032301--6cdb0ccc5e11.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0032301?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Adrienne Murray follows NASA scientists in Iceland researching a rare total solar eclipse.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Now</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0031qjy#3</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T01:00:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0031qjy--3b00970eb874.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0031qjy?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Shiona McCallum meets mums and hospital staff trialling a new assisted birth innovation.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Now</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0031d1p#3</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T01:00:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0031d1p--4e834fb3c8da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m0031d1p?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Laura Cress has the highlights from Gamescom, the biggest gaming convention in the world.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Now</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk